{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>ויישם</b> is written. This teaches that they placed a death potion in the bowl and hastened him to eat so that he would not notice." "<b>ויישם</b> — two occurrences of adjacent forms (סמיכי): here and the other ויישם בארון. A hint that they wanted to kill him and place him in a box, and he sensed it and said: \"I will not eat until I have spoken my words, for I am Abraham's servant,\" and I conducted in his household so as not to eat until I speak my words — the blessing of hand-washing, the blessing of HaMotzi. And thereby he reckoned that the cup of blessing would join for good and not for harm. And so it was for him, for an angel came and turned the death potion back toward Betuel, and he ate and died. And there are those who say: they gave him a forbidden substance, and he said: \"I will not eat until I have spoken my words — I am Abraham's servant, and I do not eat a forbidden substance.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {1 "סמיכי refers to identical or adjacent word-forms; בארון likely refers to Genesis 40:23 (ויישם בארון), though the phrase also echoes 'placed in a box/ark' which is the point of the hint. HaMotzi = the blessing over bread."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:16:51.652333581Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}